Article 16 In any of the following circumstances, registration shall not be granted:
(1) Having no civil capacity or having limited civil capacity;
(2) Having been subject to criminal punishment, where less than two years have elapsed since the completion of the execution of the punishment, or the period during which the person is prohibited from engaging in the physician profession according to law has not expired;
(3) Having been disqualified from the physician practice certificate for less than two years;
(4) Having been deregistered due to failure in the regular assessment of physicians for less than one year; or
(5) Other circumstances under which a person is not allowed to engage in medical and health services as provided for by laws or administrative regulations.
Where the health administrative department that accepts an application decides not to grant registration, it shall notify the applicant and the medical and health institution where the applicant works in writing within twenty working days from the date of accepting the application, and state the reasons.

Article 17 In any of the following circumstances after a physician's registration, the registration shall be cancelled and the physician practice certificate shall be revoked:
(1) Death;
(2) Subjection to criminal punishment;
(3) Disqualification from the physician practice certificate;
(4) Failure in the regular assessment of physicians, and upon expiration of the suspension of practice activities, failure again in a reassessment;
(5) Suspension of physician practice activities for at least two years; or
(6) Other circumstances under which the person is not allowed to engage in medical and health services or shall undergo deregistration procedures as provided for by laws or administrative regulations.
Where the circumstances specified in the preceding paragraph exist, the medical and health institution where the physician works shall report to the health administrative department that granted the registration within thirty days; where the health administrative department discovers, in the course of performing its functions, that a physician is in any circumstance specified in the preceding paragraph, it shall promptly notify the health administrative department that granted the registration. The health administrative department that granted the registration shall promptly cancel the registration and revoke the physician practice certificate.

Article 22 A physician shall enjoy the following rights in practice activities:
(1) Conducting medical examinations, disease investigations, medical treatments, issuing corresponding medical certificates, and choosing reasonable medical, prevention, and health care plans within the registered practice scope and in accordance with relevant standards;
(2) Receiving labor remuneration, enjoying the welfare benefits provided by the State, participating in social insurance in accordance with the provisions, and enjoying the corresponding benefits;
(3) Obtaining basic practice conditions and occupational protective equipment that meet the standards set by the State;
(4) Engaging in medical education, research, and academic exchanges;
(5) Participating in professional training and receiving continuing medical education;
(6) Putting forward opinions and suggestions on the work of the medical and health institution where he or she works and the health administrative department, and participating in the democratic management of the institution according to law; and
(7) Other rights provided for by laws and regulations.

Article 23 A physician shall perform the following obligations in practice activities:
(1) Cultivating a spirit of dedication, adhering to professional ethics, fulfilling the duties of a physician, doing his or her utmost to treat patients, and implementing public health measures such as epidemic prevention and control;
(2) Following clinical diagnosis and treatment guidelines, complying with clinical technical operation standards and medical ethics norms;
(3) Respecting, caring for, and protecting patients, and protecting patients' privacy and personal information according to law;
(4) Striving to study professional knowledge, updating knowledge, improving medical professional technical ability and level, and enhancing the quality of medical and health services;
(5) Propagating and popularizing health science knowledge appropriate for the post, and providing health education and health guidance to patients and the public; and
(6) Other obligations provided for by laws and regulations.

Article 33 Where any of the following circumstances occurs in practice activities, a physician shall promptly report to the medical and health institution where he or she works or to the relevant departments or institutions in accordance with the relevant provisions:
(1) Discovering infectious diseases, sudden diseases of unknown cause, or abnormal health events;
(2) Occurrence or discovery of a medical accident;
(3) Discovering adverse reactions or adverse events that may be related to drugs or medical devices;
(4) Discovering counterfeit drugs or劣质 drugs;
(5) Discovering that a patient is suspected of being involved in an injury incident or unnatural death; or
(6) Other circumstances provided for by laws or regulations.

Article 48 A physician who falls under any of the following circumstances shall be commended and rewarded in accordance with the relevant provisions of the State:
(1) Having noble medical ethics and outstanding deeds in practice activities;
(2) Having made pioneering innovations in medical research and education, made major breakthroughs in medical professional technology, and made significant contributions;
(3) Having performed outstandingly in prevention and early warning, life-saving, and other work during emergencies;
(4) Having worked diligently for a long time in medical and health institutions below the county level in difficult and remote areas;
(5) Having made outstanding contributions in disease prevention and control and health promotion; or
(6) Other circumstances provided for by laws or regulations.

Article 55 Where a physician, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts in his or her practice activities, the health administrative department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order correction and give a warning; if the circumstances are serious, the department shall order suspension of practice for not less than six months but not more than one year up to revocation of the physician practice certificate:
(1) failing to fulfill the obligation of informing or obtain informed consent in accordance with the provisions when providing medical and health services or conducting medical clinical research;
(2) refusing emergency treatment for patients requiring emergency rescue, or delaying diagnosis and treatment due to irresponsibility;
(3) failing to obey the dispatch of the health administrative department in the event of emergencies such as natural disasters, accident disasters, public health incidents, and social security incidents that seriously threaten people's life and health;
(4) failing to report the relevant circumstances in accordance with the provisions;
(5) violating laws, regulations, rules, or practice norms, causing medical accidents or other serious consequences.

Article 56 Where a physician, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts in his or her practice activities, the health administrative department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order correction, give a warning, confiscate the illegal gains, and concurrently impose a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 30,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, the department shall order suspension of practice for not less than six months but not more than one year up to revocation of the physician practice certificate:
(1) disclosing a patient's privacy or personal information;
(2) issuing false medical certificates, or signing diagnostic, therapeutic, epidemiological or other certificates or certificates concerning birth, death, etc., without personal examination or investigation;
(3) concealing, forging, altering, or destroying without authorization medical documents such as medical records and relevant materials;
(4) failing to use narcotic drugs, medical toxic drugs, psychotropic drugs, radioactive drugs, etc., in accordance with the provisions;
(5) taking advantage of the position to solicit or illegally accept property or seek other illegitimate benefits, or in violation of diagnosis and treatment standards, performing unnecessary examinations or treatments on patients causing adverse consequences;
(6) carrying out clinical application of prohibited medical technologies.
